WEBVTT

00:06.000 --> 00:07.800
Bring out Esta.

00:07.800 --> 00:09.230
Calm down, now.

00:09.480 --> 00:11.150
I am perfectly calm!

00:11.150 --> 00:12.190
Good to hear.

00:13.600 --> 00:17.800
I find it hard to believe 
that Esta was a traitor.

00:17.800 --> 00:21.370
I was hoping you woke 
me up for a good reason.

00:21.840 --> 00:25.980
If she weren't one of us, I would've 
sentenced her to lashings for heresy.

00:28.070 --> 00:33.000
Rit, I'm sure you're working with 
Esta and trying to cover for her,

00:33.000 --> 00:37.010
but it's not gonna work! I know everything!

00:39.580 --> 00:41.950
Hey, is this gonna work out?

00:42.370 --> 00:44.400
They made the first move.

00:44.400 --> 00:46.520
This might be the
 best time to play our cards.

00:46.820 --> 00:50.240
May I return to the inn? 
I haven't had breakfast yet.

00:50.240 --> 00:51.670
You're not going anywhere!

00:52.210 --> 00:53.530
Oh, fine.

00:54.620 --> 00:58.030
Why don't we go inside and talk it out?

01:11.250 --> 01:17.960
<b>Banished from the Hero's Party,
I Decided to Live a Quiet Life in the Countryside 2nd</b>

02:28.780 --> 02:33.500
<b>The Hero and
 the Guide</b>

02:28.800 --> 02:31.450
<i>We certainly didn't expect 
them to find out so soon.</i>

02:31.450 --> 02:34.000
<i>What are you going to do, Red?</i>

02:34.000 --> 02:35.560
Okay, Esta!

02:35.560 --> 02:40.760
Fess up! Say, "I'm a traitor and 
I deserve to be killed by Van."

02:41.330 --> 02:44.390
Quite frankly, I am insulted that 
you would accuse me of betrayal.

02:44.390 --> 02:48.270
I was asked to look into the 
identity of Van's target.

02:48.690 --> 02:50.620
Do you concur, Ljubo?

02:50.620 --> 02:52.340
Certainly, yes.

02:53.040 --> 02:56.740
And Rit is a =former adventurer 
based in this town,

02:56.740 --> 02:59.300
so I approached her for information.

02:59.890 --> 03:00.780
Lavender.

03:01.160 --> 03:02.280
What?

03:02.640 --> 03:06.240
Remember my partner I told 
you about? Let me introduce you.

03:09.280 --> 03:11.710
You're the swordsman who stole my shield!

03:12.220 --> 03:15.210
No! What are Gideon and Danan doing here?

03:15.560 --> 03:18.000
Who's what, now?

03:18.000 --> 03:20.030
They're members of Ruti the Hero's party.

03:20.030 --> 03:21.720
But yes, what are you doing here?

03:22.210 --> 03:25.220
As you can see, I messed up in battle.

03:25.750 --> 03:27.720
O-Oh, dear!

03:28.050 --> 03:33.000
And there you have the reason 
I came here for information.

03:33.000 --> 03:37.730
Anyone who fights the demon lord's army 
ought to have immense respect for these two.

03:38.710 --> 03:40.010
I see.

03:40.010 --> 03:43.200
But then, why did you attack me?

03:43.980 --> 03:45.070
Wha?

03:45.070 --> 03:48.720
Because you were attempting to harm people.

03:48.720 --> 03:49.500
Harm them?

03:50.070 --> 03:52.660
We may have left the Hero's party,

03:52.660 --> 03:57.000
but we still want to stop anything that 
would make the people of Zoltan suffer.

03:57.260 --> 03:59.730
Make them suffer? You misunderstand.

03:59.730 --> 04:02.080
I wanted to save them from their wayward ways

04:02.080 --> 04:06.070
and help them return to a life 
guided by their Blessings.

04:07.240 --> 04:08.260
I misunderstand, huh?

04:09.890 --> 04:12.020
You tried to use magic to control their minds

04:12.390 --> 04:15.190
and put those salt dragons 
up to attack the town.

04:18.260 --> 04:23.110
Those are problems the Hero should 
be putting a stop to, not causing.

04:23.430 --> 04:24.820
I am the Hero.

04:25.240 --> 04:29.120
I only did what my Blessing's 
impulses told me was right.

04:29.680 --> 04:34.370
As the Guide, I believe I need 
to have a long chat with you.

04:34.880 --> 04:39.520
The Guide? 
You have the Divine Blessing of the Guide?

04:39.520 --> 04:43.380
So the Almighty has tasked you with the role 
of guiding the Hero onto the right path.

04:43.880 --> 04:46.280
Yeah, though I've fulfilled 
that role already.

04:46.840 --> 04:49.390
That's why I'm here now.

04:49.690 --> 04:51.890
You've fulfilled your role?

04:52.770 --> 04:57.670
Then you shouldn't have 
anything left to live for.

04:59.490 --> 05:01.900
Yet here I am, living my own life.

05:04.030 --> 05:05.900
Stop confusing Van!

05:06.420 --> 05:07.310
Lavender.

05:07.310 --> 05:10.800
Rit, I will not let anyone 
get in the way of my love.

05:10.800 --> 05:13.540
Nobody's trying to.

05:14.000 --> 05:17.920
I just want you to know Red... 
and my love for him.

05:18.500 --> 05:23.420
I'm deeply in love with him, and the 
life I have with him here in Zoltan.

05:28.020 --> 05:31.120
This has been a profound meeting for all of us.

05:31.600 --> 05:34.940
How about we leave it at that for now?

05:34.940 --> 05:36.190
Y-Yes.

05:36.190 --> 05:40.940
Let us meet again to discuss things at a
 later date. Would that be acceptable?

05:41.500 --> 05:45.440
Yes, it's not good to talk things out 
when neither side is thinking straight.

05:55.250 --> 05:57.430
Are you sure about letting them leave?

05:57.430 --> 06:01.090
I feel like we should've pushed them 
harder while they were confused.

06:01.480 --> 06:05.220
Even if we'd fooled them, 
they would've realized later.

06:05.750 --> 06:10.000
What we need to do is change 
how Van sees the world.

06:10.000 --> 06:14.910
And what that calls for isn't 
deception, but negotiation.

06:14.910 --> 06:16.750
Sounds like a pain.

06:17.370 --> 06:21.110
I hope we can find a solution
 that Van can accept.

06:21.650 --> 06:23.110
Does such a solution even exist?

06:23.600 --> 06:25.100
Who knows?

06:25.650 --> 06:27.990
Because he's such a Blessing fundamentalist,

06:27.990 --> 06:30.810
I mean something to him as the Guide.

06:31.360 --> 06:37.020
Which is why I thought he'd hear me out 
if I talked to him about the Blessings.

06:40.320 --> 06:41.130
Delicious.

06:41.710 --> 06:43.580
I mixed in a little mead.

06:43.850 --> 06:44.380
This is great.

06:44.640 --> 06:47.430
Anyway, we have a temporary reprieve.

06:47.430 --> 06:48.880
What do we do next?

06:49.190 --> 06:53.450
Well, we need to be cautious with the talks,

06:53.450 --> 06:55.760
but I don't think we'll get many chances.

06:56.380 --> 06:59.830
He strikes me as someone who doesn't 
take long to make a decision.

07:00.400 --> 07:04.900
If only we had some way to fix 
all of this in one fell swoop.

07:05.830 --> 07:07.170
I'm stepping out for a bit.

07:09.510 --> 07:11.660
Welcome, Big Brother.

07:11.660 --> 07:13.460
You haven't had lunch yet, right?

07:13.460 --> 07:15.960
You made lunch for me? Thank you.

07:15.960 --> 07:17.660
They're just sandwiches.

07:18.320 --> 07:20.090
I'm excited for dinner, too.

07:22.320 --> 07:23.920
About that...

07:24.540 --> 07:27.910
I think I should avoid 
coming here for a while.

07:28.380 --> 07:30.960
Why? Because of Lavender's ability?

07:30.960 --> 07:35.430
Yeah, she seems surprisingly adept at 
determining a person's location.

07:36.020 --> 07:39.160
There's no telling when she'll 
figure out where you are.

07:39.160 --> 07:39.930
I see.

07:40.420 --> 07:42.940
What's more, we met Van's party today.

07:43.980 --> 07:44.940
Oh...

07:49.160 --> 07:49.940
Ruti?

07:50.540 --> 07:55.720
I guess the Almighty really 
won't let me live a normal life.

07:55.720 --> 08:00.360
Maybe Lord Demis is hoping that 
the Hero who cast her role aside

08:00.360 --> 08:03.980
will be defeated by a new Hero.

08:06.680 --> 08:10.090
But, by preventing you two from fighting,

08:10.710 --> 08:14.660
I think we can throw a wrench in those plans.

08:16.320 --> 08:18.130
Wouldn't that be satisfying?

08:21.160 --> 08:23.020
You really are something else.

08:24.840 --> 08:27.770
Ruti, Tisse, are you in?

08:28.910 --> 08:30.550
Oh, Megria.

08:31.120 --> 08:32.370
Come in.

08:32.370 --> 08:37.780
Don't mind me. I just wanted to 
share some news while passing by.

08:38.080 --> 08:39.740
What news?

08:39.740 --> 08:40.790
Well...

08:41.120 --> 08:46.540
Someone has accepted the 
herb-collecting request you two posted.

08:46.870 --> 08:50.940
That's great. Now we can grow more herbs.

08:50.940 --> 08:53.150
Thanks for letting us know.

08:53.150 --> 08:54.480
No problem.

08:54.480 --> 08:56.080
Just who I wanted to see.

08:56.080 --> 08:59.050
I was about to head out to the 
Adventurers' Guild, actually.

08:59.310 --> 09:01.560
Huh? Why's that?

09:02.020 --> 09:04.580
I wanted to see if you had 
any interesting missions.

09:04.580 --> 09:06.280
Interesting?

09:07.650 --> 09:12.070
Preferably something that mainly involves 
exploring, with a side of combat.

09:12.380 --> 09:15.940
We're in Zoltan. 
There aren't going to be any—

09:15.940 --> 09:17.380
Oh, great!

09:17.380 --> 09:18.530
You have something?

09:18.530 --> 09:21.430
Some dangerous monsters were spotted nearby.

09:21.430 --> 09:24.790
And if there's a herd of them, we don't 
have anyone able to deal with them.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.170
Tell me more.

09:27.610 --> 09:30.040
Of course. I'll give you all the details.

09:30.580 --> 09:34.020
Could you come with me
 to the Adventurers' Guild?

09:34.020 --> 09:37.050
I'd like to formally request 
that you take the job.

09:37.660 --> 09:41.050
So, yeah, I went and accepted a mission.

09:41.890 --> 09:45.060
Sea bogies? Those are pretty rare.

09:45.060 --> 09:48.140
I hate those things.

09:48.140 --> 09:49.890
Can't stand the sight of them.

09:49.890 --> 09:52.150
I don't think anyone can.

09:52.150 --> 09:55.400
Their very existence deals 
psychic damage to people.

09:55.400 --> 09:58.780
I wouldn't know. I kill them on sight.

09:59.090 --> 10:04.780
They emit a terrifying aura that affects 
our minds and drains our life force.

10:04.780 --> 10:08.500
The biggest problem is that they 
target human children and eat them.

10:09.280 --> 10:11.250
Gotta take 'em out.

10:11.520 --> 10:16.190
According to Megria, only a few 
of them were spotted nearby.

10:16.190 --> 10:18.260
But I want to take care of this quickly.

10:18.680 --> 10:21.260
Okay, but what about Van?

10:21.790 --> 10:24.260
I was thinking of asking him 
to join the mission, actually.

10:24.640 --> 10:27.140
What?!

10:27.540 --> 10:29.980
You wanna fight alongside that punk?!

10:29.980 --> 10:31.650
Red, are you out of your mind?!

10:32.220 --> 10:36.890
Van prioritizes raising his 
Blessing's level over saving lives.

10:36.890 --> 10:39.530
He might cause some serious problems.

10:40.560 --> 10:43.340
I think it's a good idea, though.

10:43.340 --> 10:48.730
I felt that Lavender needs to get a 
closer look at what Red and I are like.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.550
And this might be a good chance.

10:52.280 --> 10:53.550
Lavender, huh?

10:54.410 --> 10:57.330
It'd be nice to get a better 
understanding of her abilities, too.

10:57.330 --> 10:58.420
Makes sense.

10:59.090 --> 11:02.720
So, you're hoping fighting 
together will tell ya something!

11:02.720 --> 11:05.430
In that case, count me in.

11:05.430 --> 11:07.810
Nah, it'll just be Rit and me.

11:09.840 --> 11:12.310
You're asking me to hold down the fort?!

11:12.560 --> 11:13.320
Sorry, man.

11:20.720 --> 11:24.580
Danan's over-the-top reaction surprised me.

11:24.580 --> 11:25.580
I see.

11:27.200 --> 11:28.330
Is something wrong?

11:28.900 --> 11:33.940
I want to be of help to Big Brother, 
but I'm not able to.

11:34.600 --> 11:37.310
And that's a little frustrating.

11:38.330 --> 11:39.720
Miss Ruti...

11:47.530 --> 11:51.020
I'm glad you agreed to help out. 
I thought you'd refuse.

11:51.630 --> 11:54.270
It's the Hero's duty to slay evil.

11:56.100 --> 11:58.640
The beach in the reports is up ahead.

11:58.640 --> 12:00.000
Get ready.

12:00.500 --> 12:04.700
I am ready right now. 
The Hero is always prepared to fight.

12:05.290 --> 12:08.410
Fighting's just a part of life for you, huh?

12:09.040 --> 12:11.660
Isn't that true for all living 
creatures in this world?

12:12.050 --> 12:15.420
So long as we have Blessings, 
none of us can avoid fighting...

12:22.580 --> 12:23.850
I think.

12:24.880 --> 12:28.120
What are you talking about, Van? 
Let's hurry up and go.

12:28.120 --> 12:28.970
Right.

12:29.540 --> 12:32.930
So, Gideon and I will take point 
and fight. Is that correct?

12:33.290 --> 12:34.000
Yeah.

12:34.550 --> 12:37.260
Rit and Lavender, cover us with your magic.

12:37.260 --> 12:38.440
You got it, Red.

12:38.810 --> 12:42.690
Why do I have to take orders from you?

12:47.300 --> 12:50.360
It looks like there aren't many of them,

12:50.360 --> 12:52.340
but there are some hiding by the rocks.

12:52.340 --> 12:53.910
A fair few of them, even.

12:53.910 --> 12:55.610
They're not very strong,

12:55.610 --> 12:57.500
but stay alert, Van.

12:58.950 --> 13:01.170
Why are you using a bronze sword?

13:03.160 --> 13:08.240
I don't need expensive equipment, now that 
I'm no longer fighting to save the world.

13:08.240 --> 13:11.830
But you're forced to fight 
for as long as you live.

13:11.830 --> 13:12.350
Right.

13:13.020 --> 13:15.850
Which is why I carry a bronze sword around.

13:17.790 --> 13:21.070
I still don't understand why you 
would wield an inferior weapon.

13:21.070 --> 13:26.860
But surely it was Lord Demis's will 
that brought you before me to guide me.

13:27.610 --> 13:28.680
Nah, I—

13:28.680 --> 13:30.620
Looks like they've noticed us.

13:33.640 --> 13:34.790
Let's do this.

13:50.310 --> 13:54.140
They're nothing special, 
but the Hero must slay all evil!

13:58.080 --> 13:59.700
Get ready!

14:13.020 --> 14:13.620
Van!

14:17.880 --> 14:18.920
Are you okay?

14:18.920 --> 14:21.420
Gideon, you don't need to worry about me.

14:21.760 --> 14:25.040
You fight assuming you'll 
use Healing Hands later.

14:25.040 --> 14:26.420
Do you not defend yourself?

14:26.990 --> 14:30.450
Offense is the best defense, is it not?

14:33.080 --> 14:35.160
Nothing wrong with avoiding 
getting hurt for no reason.

14:35.160 --> 14:37.650
I refuse to pull any punches 
in my battles against evil.

14:37.650 --> 14:39.750
That is how the Hero must fight.

14:40.200 --> 14:44.300
I don't think adapting your fighting style to
 your opponents counts as pulling punches.

14:45.480 --> 14:47.420
Whatever. Let's keep going.

14:47.420 --> 14:48.120
Yes.

15:04.800 --> 15:08.300
Van, did you keep count?

15:08.640 --> 15:09.220
Huh?

15:09.660 --> 15:11.510
How many monsters did you kill?

15:11.840 --> 15:14.560
Is there any need to?

15:14.560 --> 15:17.400
The Hero need only slay evil.

15:17.400 --> 15:19.020
It doesn't matter how many.

15:19.520 --> 15:22.240
There were 45 sea bogies in total.

15:22.240 --> 15:26.000
I killed 26, you 18, and Rit got one.

15:26.000 --> 15:27.530
So what?

15:27.820 --> 15:29.720
The number of enemies you take down

15:29.720 --> 15:34.030
can be a marker of your 
contributions in battle.

15:34.570 --> 15:35.270
That's...

15:35.270 --> 15:37.820
You're supposed to be the 
Hero, the strongest.

15:37.820 --> 15:40.440
So you'd better fix this quickly.

15:43.600 --> 15:46.190
The Divine Blessing of the 
Guide shows the Hero the way.

15:46.190 --> 15:47.050
Right.

15:47.050 --> 15:50.070
Which means, until you 
surpass me in every way,

15:50.070 --> 15:53.050
you won't be the finished 
article as the Hero.

15:54.160 --> 15:56.800
That's what I believe, but what about you?

15:59.530 --> 16:01.860
You may well be right.

16:03.060 --> 16:03.940
Van!

16:04.850 --> 16:06.310
Why, you!

16:06.830 --> 16:08.850
Hey, all I did was give my opinion.

16:08.850 --> 16:12.320
Listen, Van. 
You're fine just the way you are.

16:12.670 --> 16:16.620
<i>A partner who accepts everything, 
including your weaknesses.</i>

16:17.220 --> 16:19.580
<i>Feels like that'd just ruin a person.</i>

16:19.910 --> 16:20.710
What?!

16:20.710 --> 16:22.540
Uh, I didn't say a thing.

16:22.540 --> 16:25.600
Anyway, the evil is slain. Let us return.

16:25.600 --> 16:26.540
Wait.

16:26.940 --> 16:28.550
There are more sea bogies around.

16:28.870 --> 16:29.950
What?

16:37.590 --> 16:40.460
I have no idea what you're talking about.

16:40.460 --> 16:43.060
There are tracks that head 
towards the village and return.

16:43.420 --> 16:44.540
The village?

16:44.540 --> 16:46.730
That's how they act when 
they abduct children.

16:47.660 --> 16:50.780
They've probably already abducted a child.

16:50.780 --> 16:54.780
And maybe seeing that child was what made 
the other sea bogies head toward the village.

16:55.080 --> 16:57.020
We must rescue the child at once!

16:57.020 --> 16:59.530
Van, can you follow tracks?

17:01.380 --> 17:02.540
I cannot.

17:03.130 --> 17:06.810
I haven't acquired the skill, 
for it is unneeded in battle.

17:07.440 --> 17:09.540
Okay. Rit and I can handle it.

17:09.850 --> 17:13.920
My Blessing makes me really good at 
following tracks, so don't worry.

17:14.190 --> 17:16.490
Don't make that face, "Hero."

17:16.490 --> 17:19.930
Just be happy that we're here to do that job.

17:20.990 --> 17:21.890
Okay.

17:21.890 --> 17:24.430
Hey, stop messing with my Van!

17:25.170 --> 17:26.620
It's okay, Van!

17:26.620 --> 17:28.190
You don't need a tracking skill.

17:28.190 --> 17:31.900
I can detect all living creatures 
wherever the wind can go!

17:42.340 --> 17:44.960
Sea bogies don't devour 
children immediately.

17:44.960 --> 17:47.420
They feed off their fear first.

17:48.450 --> 17:49.750
I hope there's still time.

17:50.660 --> 17:52.450
I sense sea bogies.

17:52.450 --> 17:53.610
I'll go ahead.

18:11.210 --> 18:14.350
It's okay. Sea bogies can't hear very well.

18:14.350 --> 18:16.990
Though being stealthy is never a bad thing.

18:18.100 --> 18:19.560
Do you see any kids?

18:19.560 --> 18:20.990
Not from here.

18:27.110 --> 18:29.710
There are two in front, 
and three in the back.

18:29.970 --> 18:30.670
I'll go!

18:43.760 --> 18:44.890
Are you all right?

18:44.890 --> 18:45.820
Yes.

18:45.820 --> 18:47.450
Okay, good.

18:47.920 --> 18:50.470
Let's split up and look for the kid.

19:04.990 --> 19:05.950
Are you all right?

19:07.430 --> 19:10.170
I am Van the Hero. I am here to save you.

19:10.840 --> 19:13.420
The... Hero?

19:13.730 --> 19:14.920
Yes, that's right!

19:20.710 --> 19:22.680
Sir Hero!

19:23.300 --> 19:24.930
Hey! Get off him!

19:25.420 --> 19:27.190
I said, get off!

19:25.920 --> 19:29.930
I was so scared, Sir Hero!

19:27.690 --> 19:29.930
Van, you push her off!

19:32.750 --> 19:34.940
Thank you so much!

19:34.940 --> 19:37.980
I don't know how to repay you!

19:37.980 --> 19:42.080
If it weren't for you, she would be...

19:44.680 --> 19:46.220
No need for thanks.

19:46.220 --> 19:47.500
Sir Hero.

19:48.390 --> 19:50.710
Thank you for saving me!

19:55.340 --> 19:58.210
Oh? Van, of all people?

19:58.740 --> 20:01.510
He listened to advice?

20:01.810 --> 20:04.470
There, there. It's like that sometimes.

20:05.610 --> 20:09.060
I'm amazed you can get through 
to Lavender, too, Rit.

20:09.290 --> 20:10.130
Huh?

20:11.050 --> 20:14.740
Well, we have something in common.

20:15.470 --> 20:19.070
We are both in love, you know!

20:20.900 --> 20:23.200
I can't do anything right.

20:23.520 --> 20:24.450
What do you mean?

20:24.450 --> 20:29.590
I had plenty of chances to talk to 
Van and Lavender during our travels,

20:29.590 --> 20:33.510
but I couldn't change their 
thinking in any way whatsoever.

20:34.140 --> 20:38.490
But you two managed to do 
just that in such a short time.

20:38.490 --> 20:40.420
It's enough to make one lose all confidence.

20:40.720 --> 20:42.350
Well, you shouldn't!

20:42.350 --> 20:44.680
You're the one who made all of this happen!

20:46.320 --> 20:47.680
Really?

20:47.970 --> 20:49.130
Of course!

20:49.130 --> 20:54.190
All of this started because 
you sent me to Red!

20:55.490 --> 20:56.650
R-Right...

20:57.260 --> 20:59.770
You wore a mask and hid 
everything about yourself,

20:59.770 --> 21:03.820
but I know exactly just how 
hard you've been trying!

21:04.070 --> 21:10.080
M-Mm. As long as you understand, 
that's fine by me.

21:10.840 --> 21:11.830
I do!

21:12.400 --> 21:13.830
They make a fine duo.

21:14.190 --> 21:15.580
D-Don't be ridiculous!

21:16.190 --> 21:17.040
"Ridiculous"?

21:17.350 --> 21:18.690
No, wait!

21:18.690 --> 21:22.510
I did not mean to say you're 
unfit to be my partner!

21:24.440 --> 21:25.560
It's just, uh...

21:26.010 --> 21:29.990
Of course. I still have a long way to go.

21:29.990 --> 21:31.510
I'll do my best!

21:31.510 --> 21:32.970
No!

21:32.970 --> 21:35.230
Wait, that's not a bad thing, but still...

21:35.920 --> 21:37.690
Oh, for the love of...!

21:38.810 --> 21:40.480
That's about all the sweetness I can take.

21:40.480 --> 21:41.650
Same here.

21:41.650 --> 21:43.240
Like you two can talk!

21:43.240 --> 21:44.440
Why?!

21:43.240 --> 21:44.440
Why not?!

21:44.690 --> 21:45.700
Huh?

21:47.780 --> 21:50.500
You two are always like this!

21:50.500 --> 21:52.040
Not true.

21:50.500 --> 21:52.040
That's not true.

22:02.720 --> 22:04.130
The Hero does not lose his way.

22:05.370 --> 22:06.770
Never, ever.
